      "source": [
        "# Soybean Rust Early Warning — Phase 2, Notebook 1: Sowing dates from season onset\n",
        "\n",
        "**Why this notebook:** a rust-risk map needs a sowing date for every grid cell, so that R4 and the 14-day weather window can be placed.\n",
        "Nobody recorded sowing dates for grid cells, so they will be estimated from **season onset**: the date the rains properly start.\n",
        "\n",
        "**What it does:** applies season-onset rules to daily **CHIRPS** rainfall (0.05°, about 5.5 km) at the trial sites and compares the\n",
        "predicted onset with the **recorded sowing dates** of the PAT trials. This tests each rule before it is used on the map.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Which trials:** rainy-season (season 2) trials in Malawi and Zambia that were **rainfed** or **supplementary** (initially rainfed).\n",
        "Irrigated and dry-season trials are excluded, because their planting was not driven by the rains.\n",
        "\n",
        "**The key comparison:** a rule is only useful if it predicts sowing better than simply assuming the **typical sowing date** every year.\n",
        "Both are evaluated fairly: the typical date and the typical onset-to-sowing gap are always learned from the **other** years.\n",
        "\n",
      
      ]
    },
    {
