      "source": [
        "## 5. How to read the result\n",
        "\n",
        "* If **onset + gap** has a clearly lower MAE than the **fixed date**, onset captures real year-to-year and place-to-place differences in planting, and the map should use it.\n",
        "* If the fixed date is as good or better, trial planting did not follow the rains closely (researchers often plant on schedule), and a simpler fixed sowing date is defensible for the first maps. Farmers' fields may still follow onset more closely than research trials.\n",
        "* Rules A and B include a **false-start check**; rule C does not. Comparing them shows whether the check matters here.\n",
        "* Dr. Francis's script can be added as another rule and compared on exactly the same trials."
      ]
    },
